To insulate your core domain from carrier SDK model leakage across 19 files, adopt the **Ports and Adapters (Hexagonal Architecture)** pattern combined with an **Anti-Corruption Layer (ACL)** and **Polymorphic Strategy Dispatch**.

---

### Architectural Design Overview

```
                                 +-----------------------------------+
                                 |            Core Domain            |
                                 |  (Pure TypeScript, 0 SDK Imports) |
                                 |                                   |
                                 |  +-----------------------------+  |
                                 |  |     ShippingCarrierPort     |  |
                                 |  |  (Domain Interface Contract)|  |
                                 |  +--------------+--------------+  |
                                 +-----------------|-----------------+
                                                   | Implemented by
                                                   v
     +-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
     |                               Infrastructure Layer                                |
     |                                                                                   |
     |  +--------------------+     +-------------------+     +-------------------------+ |
     |  |    FedExAdapter    |     |    UPSAdapter     |     |       DHLAdapter        | |
     |  | +----------------+ |     | +---------------+ |     | +---------------------+ | |
     |  | | FedEx Mappers  | |     | |  UPS Mappers  | |     | |     DHL Mappers     | | |
     |  | +----------------+ |     | +---------------+ |     | +---------------------+ | |
     |  +---------+----------+     +---------+---------+     +------------+------------+ |
     +------------|--------------------------|----------------------------|--------------+
                  v                          v                            v
          FedEx SDK / API               UPS SDK / API               DHL SDK / API
```

1. **Core Domain (`src/domain/shipping/`)**: Defines pure TypeScript domain entities, Value Objects, unified Result error types, and the `ShippingCarrierPort` interface. Zero imports from SDKs or vendor libraries are permitted.
2. **Anti-Corruption Layer Adapters (`src/infrastructure/carriers/`)**: Wraps carrier-specific SDKs. Each carrier gets an isolated directory (e.g., `fedex/`, `ups/`, `dhl/`) containing adapters and mapping functions that translate external payloads into domain models.
3. **Polymorphic Strategy Dispatch (`src/application/carrier-service.ts`)**: Replaces nested `if (carrier === 'FEDEX')` blocks with a carrier registry executing standard interface contracts.

---

### Concrete TypeScript Implementation

#### 1. Core Domain Models & Port Interface

```typescript
// src/domain/shipping/types.ts
export interface Money {
  readonly amount: number;
  readonly currency: string;
}

export interface Address {
  readonly street: string;
  readonly city: string;
  readonly postalCode: string;
  readonly countryCode: string;
}

export interface RateQuoteRequest {
  readonly origin: Address;
  readonly destination: Address;
  readonly weightKg: number;
}

export interface ShippingRate {
  readonly carrierId: string;
  readonly serviceName: string;
  readonly totalCost: Money;
  readonly estimatedDays: number;
}

export type CarrierError =
  | { readonly kind: "RateLimitExceeded"; readonly carrier: string; readonly retryAfterMs?: number }
  | { readonly kind: "InvalidAddress"; readonly carrier: string; readonly details: string }
  | { readonly kind: "NetworkFailure"; readonly carrier: string; readonly cause: Error }
  | { readonly kind: "ProviderError"; readonly carrier: string; readonly code: string; readonly message: string };

export type Result<T, E> =
  | { readonly ok: true; readonly value: T }
  | { readonly ok: false; readonly error: E };
