---

### 3. Tradeoffs

| Category | Benefit | Cost / Tradeoff |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Domain Safety** | Core business logic is immune to vendor API changes or SDK version upgrades. | Initial mapping overhead for complex nested carrier DTOs. |
| **Testability** | Unit tests in domain files mock `ShippingCarrierPort` without SDK dependencies. | Extra type definitions required in the core domain layer. |
| **Extensibility** | Adding a 4th carrier (e.g., USPS) requires 0 edits to core domain files. | Lowest-common-denominator domain models may hide niche vendor features. |
| **Maintainability** | SDK breaking changes are contained entirely within 1 adapter file per vendor. | Must maintain explicit bidirectional ACL mappers. |

---

### 4. Reversible Adoption Plan

To refactor the 19 domain files without risky big-bang deployments, follow this 4-phase plan with explicit rollback seams.

```
Phase 1: Ports & ACL Interfaces (Side-by-side)
  └── Phase 2: Infrastructure Adapters & Mappers
        └── Phase 3: Strangler Fig Migration (File-by-file)
